Template: autosync/install-dir
Type: string
Default: /opt/autosync
Description: Installation directory for AutoSync:
 AutoSync's application files, Docker Compose project, and the .env
 configuration will be deployed into this directory. It must be
 writable by root and have enough free disk space for Docker volumes
 (database, uploaded documents, the local LLM model).

Template: autosync/public-host
Type: string
Default:
Description: Public hostname or IP address for accessing AutoSync:
 This is the address browsers will use to reach the AutoSync web UI
 and API — for example this server's LAN IP or a DNS name. Leave
 empty to auto-detect the machine's primary IP address.
 .
 Get this wrong and the web UI will load but fail to talk to the API
 for anyone connecting from another machine — it can be fixed later by
 editing .env in the install directory and running
 `docker compose up -d --build frontend`.

Template: autosync/frontend-port
Type: string
Default: 5173
Description: Port to expose the AutoSync web UI on:

Template: autosync/pull-llm-model
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Download the qwen2.5:14b LLM model now (~9 GB)?
 AutoSync uses a local LLM (served via Ollama) for price suggestions
 and repair-order matching. The default model is roughly 9 GB and can
 take a long time to download depending on your connection.
 .
 If you decline, AutoSync still starts and everything except
 LLM-powered features works immediately. Pull the model later with:
 docker compose exec ollama ollama pull qwen2.5:14b

Template: autosync/admin-email
Type: string
Default: admin@autosync.local
Description: Email address for the initial administrator account:

Template: autosync/admin-password
Type: password
Description: Password for the initial administrator account:
 Leave empty to generate a random password automatically — it will be
 printed at the end of installation and saved to
 INITIAL_ADMIN_CREDENTIALS.txt in the installation directory.
